class:: BlipKernel
summary:: Rectangular, triangular, or cosine-tapered finite harmonic kernel
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/BlipExtensions, Classes/BlipAD, Classes/BlipDecay, Classes/BlipDiff, Classes/BlipDisp, Classes/BlipFB, Classes/BlipFrac, Classes/BlipInt, Classes/BlipPM, Classes/BlipPeak, Classes/BlipPower, Classes/BlipSeries, Classes/BlipWidth

description::

BlipKernel changes pulse shape by weighting the first code::numharm::
harmonics. code::\rect:: uses equal weights, code::\triangle:: decreases
weights linearly, and code::\cosine:: uses a cosine-power taper.

Rectangular and triangular modes use closed forms. Cosine mode expands integer
powers 1 through 8 into at most nine shifted finite sums; fractional
code::curve:: values interpolate adjacent weight sets. Cost therefore does not
grow with harmonic count. code::amount:: mixes the weights before
renormalization and is sample accurate. Harmonic-count changes fade over one
block. All three modes retain only harmonics below the Nyquist safety margin;
their linear weight laws do not create new sidebands.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Blip::. Rectangular mode and
code::amount = 0:: reproduce its equal-weight spectrum; the tapered modes
trade a wider main pulse for lower sidelobes.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Frequency in Hz. Audio or control rate; signed values are valid.

argument:: numharm
Requested harmonic count, sampled once per block and clipped to code::1..2048::
before Nyquist limiting.

argument:: kernel
Initialization-rate selector: code::\rect::, code::\triangle::, or
code::\cosine::. Recreate the Synth to change it.

argument:: amount
Audio- or control-rate interpolation from equal weights at zero to the
selected kernel at one. Values are clipped to code::0..1::.

argument:: curve
Cosine power, sampled once per block and clipped to code::1..8::.

argument:: mul
Post-processing multiplier.

argument:: add
Post-processing offset.

examples::

code::
(
{ BlipKernel.ar(90, 40, \triangle, 1, mul: 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ BlipKernel.ar(90, 40, \cosine, 1, 4, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ BlipKernel.ar(70, 60, \triangle, SinOsc.ar(0.1).range(0, 1), mul: 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
// Modulating all parameters for a dynamic sound
(
{ BlipKernel.ar(LFNoise1.kr(1).exprange(50, 400), MouseY.kr(1, 100), \cosine, SinOsc.kr(0.5).range(0, 1), MouseX.kr(1, 8)) ! 2 * 0.1 }.play;
)
::
